- [fields.mjs](/output/lib/whoosh/fields.mjs:1)
- [test3.mjs](/output/test3.mjs:1)

The CLI parser matches the observed `argparse` behavior for `--a`, `--a=...`, required-argument failures, help/abbreviated help, explicit help arguments, and unrecognized extras. The Whoosh-side reimplementation prints exactly `<Schema: ['content']>`.

**Entry**
```js
import { parseTest3Args } from './lib/cli/parser.mjs';
import { resolveOrExit } from './lib/cli/runner.mjs';
import { StemmingAnalyzer } from './lib/whoosh/analysis.mjs';
import { Schema, TEXT } from './lib/whoosh/fields.mjs';

export function main(argv = process.argv.slice(2), scriptPath = process.argv[1]) {
  const parseResult = parseTest3Args(argv, scriptPath);
  resolveOrExit(parseResult);

  const analyzer = new StemmingAnalyzer();
  const schema = new Schema({ content: TEXT({ analyzer }) });
  console.log(schema);
}

main();
```

Verified with `node /output/test3.mjs --a foo`, `--help`, missing `--a`, missing value, unrecognized args, and help edge cases.
